## Worksheet

**F1 – Core loop**: `mulberry32(seed)` seeds `gameState.rng`, used for all randomness (fireEvent, generateCaravan, randInt); `endTurn()` runs needs→production→events→trade→hazard→win/lose in fixed order. Score 2.

**F2 – Map**: `generateMap(seed)` builds 64-tile terrain from seeded rng; `checkBuildable` enforces `building.terrain.includes(terrain)`; `getAdjacencyBonus` folds into `totalMult` in `calculateProduction`, changing `b.output`. Score 2.

**F3 – Economy**: production/consumption computed separately in `resolveBuildingProduction`; `b.output` (computed in `calculateProduction`) is never gated by whether inputs are actually available — consumption just drains stock in parallel. Caps/overflow handled via `resourceAccum`. Score 1.

**F4 – Population**: `initColonists()` creates records with skill/fatigue/morale/job/assignment; `calculateProduction` reads `c.skill`, `c.fatigue`, `getJobBonus(c.job)`. Score 2.

**F5 – Needs**: `resolvePopulationNeeds` deducts food/water and drops morale on shortage; but `calculateProduction`'s `skillMult` never reads `c.morale`, so morale changes don't affect output. Score 1.

**F6 – Research**: 8 nodes in `RESEARCH_NODES`; `unlockResearch` enforces prereqs and deducts cost; `buildingBonus`/`damageReduction`/`stormReduction` are read elsewhere, but `synthesis`'s `metalToWater` effect is never read anywhere. Score 1.

**F7 – Events**: 10 entries in `EVENTS`; `fireEvent` does weighted selection filtered by `cooldowns[e.id]===0`; cooldowns decremented every `endTurn`; all 10 events have 2 differentiated choices. Score 2.

**F8 – Trade**: `initTrade` sets static `globalPrices`, never updated afterward; `generateCaravan` only adds `randInt(-1,1)` noise, not tied to stockpiles/supply drift; `tradeCaravanBuy`/`Sell` wired via inline `onclick` and both work. Score 1.

**F9 – Hazard**: `checkAndResolveStorm` scales `severity` with turn and reduces `b.hp`; `calculateProduction` never references `b.hp`, so damaged buildings produce at full rate; `repairBuilding` spends parts and restores hp. Score 1.

**F10 – Save/load**: `serializeState`/`deserializeState` round-trip full state; `deserializeState` try/catches JSON parse and `alert`s on bad input; wired to save/load buttons. Score 2.

**F11 – End conditions**: `endTurn` sets `gameStatus` to `'won'`/`'lost'`; `showGameOver` computes `total_score` from population/research/resources/turn and renders modal. Score 2.

**F12 – UI**: tab click listeners wired; log entries carry `T${entry.turn}`; keydown handles Space + 1-5 shortcuts; no `@media` rule anywhere in the stylesheet — layout does not adapt to narrow screens. Score 1.

**F13 – Dev panel**: `runTests()` has 15 real invariant assertions incl. save/load hash equality; `runBenchmark()` drives 200 turns headlessly via a greedy policy and returns `hashState()` output. Score 2.

**G1**: `node.effects.buildingBonus` set on unlock, read as `researchBonus` in `calculateProduction`, folded into `totalMult`/`b.output` every turn. Score 4.

**G2**: `resolvePopulationNeeds` writes real morale drop on shortage, but `calculateProduction` never reads `c.morale` — final link (reduced labor output) absent. Score 1.

**G3**: `checkAndResolveStorm` damages `b.hp`; `calculateProduction` ignores `hp` entirely (full-rate output); `repairBuilding` spends parts and restores hp — output-loss link missing per explicit rubric example. Score 1.

**G4**: `globalPrices` set once in `initTrade` and never mutated; `generateCaravan` only adds `randInt(gameState.rng,-1,1)` noise, no read of `gameState.resources` or a drifting supply variable. Score 0.

**G5**: `applyEventChoice` writes distinct resource/morale/population deltas per choice (e.g. dust storm's Hunker Down vs Venture Out; water shortage's Ration vs Deep Drilling) directly into `gameState.resources`/colonists. Score 4.

